IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g7-regulations`

-- g7-tests-regulations.l4: tests of sections 59 and 60 (the Minister's powers to set fees and make regulations).
--
-- Written by ENCODER G7.  Expected values come from the SOURCE, decided before any run:
--   s.59  the Minister, WITH the approval of the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee, may set fees for application,
--         grant or renewal, final-certificate examinations including objections, and the section 17 training, and a
--         different rate for the foreign expert's temporary licence: its application or renewal, and its grant.
--         Six "for" phrases, so six heads.
--   s.60(1)  regulations on any matter connected with implementation, including heads (a), (b) and (c), WITH the
--            committee's approval; head (c) also needs consultation with the Minister concerned.
--   s.60(2)  regulations on (a) the manner of applying for a licence or renewal and (b) the manner of applying for a
--            foreign expert's temporary licence or renewal: with NO approval and no consultation.

§ `Tests of sections 59 and 60`

§§ `Fixtures: the four combinations of the two procedural facts`

GIVETH A `Procedure of the Minister's regulations`
`neither approval nor consultation` MEANS
    `Procedure of the Minister's regulations` WITH
        `the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee approved the regulations` IS FALSE
        `the Minister consulted the Minister concerned with the fields of the testers or experts` IS FALSE

GIVETH A `Procedure of the Minister's regulations`
`approval only` MEANS
    `Procedure of the Minister's regulations` WITH
        `the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee approved the regulations` IS TRUE
        `the Minister consulted the Minister concerned with the fields of the testers or experts` IS FALSE

GIVETH A `Procedure of the Minister's regulations`
`consultation only` MEANS
    `Procedure of the Minister's regulations` WITH
        `the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee approved the regulations` IS FALSE
        `the Minister consulted the Minister concerned with the fields of the testers or experts` IS TRUE

GIVETH A `Procedure of the Minister's regulations`
`approval and consultation` MEANS
    `Procedure of the Minister's regulations` WITH
        `the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee approved the regulations` IS TRUE
        `the Minister consulted the Minister concerned with the fields of the testers or experts` IS TRUE

GIVETH A `Calendar of rest days`
`the calendar with Saturday 21 March 2026 as a day of rest` MEANS
    `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS LIST YMD 2026 3 21

§§ `Section 59: the heads and the approval`

-- Six heads: four in the first sentence, two in the second.
#ASSERT count `s 59 — the heads of fee for which the Minister may set a fee` EQUALS 6
#ASSERT count `s 59 — the heads of fee for which a different rate may be set for a foreign expert's temporary licence` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `s 59 — the Law lets the Minister set a fee for` `a fee for submitting an application for a licence`
#ASSERT `s 59 — the Law lets the Minister set a fee for` `a fee for the grant of a licence, or for its renewal`
#ASSERT `s 59 — the Law lets the Minister set a fee for` `a fee for the examinations required for a final certificate, including an objection to an examination`
#ASSERT `s 59 — the Law lets the Minister set a fee for` `a fee for the continuing training under section 17`
#ASSERT `s 59 — the Law lets the Minister set a fee for` `a different rate of fee for submitting an application for a temporary licence for a foreign expert, or for its renewal`
#ASSERT `s 59 — the Law lets the Minister set a fee for` `a different rate of fee for the grant of a temporary licence for a foreign expert`
-- The two special-rate heads are among the six.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN h YIELD elem h `s 59 — the heads of fee for which the Minister may set a fee`) `s 59 — the heads of fee for which a different rate may be set for a foreign expert's temporary licence`

-- The Minister needs the committee's approval to set fees, whatever else is done.
#ASSERT `s 59 — the approval the Minister needs to set fees has been given` `approval only`
#ASSERT `s 59 — the approval the Minister needs to set fees has been given` `approval and consultation`
#ASSERT NOT `s 59 — the approval the Minister needs to set fees has been given` `neither approval nor consultation`
-- Consultation is not what section 59 asks for: without approval the power is not open.
#ASSERT NOT `s 59 — the approval the Minister needs to set fees has been given` `consultation only`

-- The power, exercised: with approval the permission stands and is fulfilled when the Minister acts; without, nothing is permitted.
#TRACE `s 59 — the Minister's power to set a fee by regulations for` `a fee for submitting an application for a licence` `, given the procedure` `approval only` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `set a fee by regulations` `a fee for submitting an application for a licence` AT 5
#TRACE `s 59 — the Minister's power to set a fee by regulations for` `a fee for submitting an application for a licence` `, given the procedure` `approval only` AT 0 WITH
    -- no events: the permission stands unused, which a MAY does not breach
#TRACE `s 59 — the Minister's power to set a fee by regulations for` `a fee for the continuing training under section 17` `, given the procedure` `neither approval nor consultation` AT 0 WITH
    -- no approval, so there is no permission to exercise

§§ `Section 60: where approval and consultation are required`

-- 60(1) and its heads (a), (b), (c): approval required.  60(2)(a), (b): not required.
#ASSERT `s 60 — the approval of the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee is required for regulations on` `any matter connected with the implementation of the Law`
#ASSERT `s 60 — the approval of the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee is required for regulations on` `the requirements of training for a licence`
#ASSERT `s 60 — the approval of the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee is required for regulations on` `the rules on the examinations required for a final certificate, including objections`
#ASSERT `s 60 — the approval of the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee is required for regulations on` `the conditions for serving as testers or experts`
#ASSERT NOT `s 60 — the approval of the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee is required for regulations on` `the manner of applying for a licence or its renewal, and the time for applying to renew`
#ASSERT NOT `s 60 — the approval of the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee is required for regulations on` `the manner of applying for a temporary licence for a foreign expert, or for its renewal`

-- Consultation: only head (c).
#ASSERT `s 60(1)(c) — consultation with the Minister concerned is required for regulations on` `the conditions for serving as testers or experts`
#ASSERT NOT `s 60(1)(c) — consultation with the Minister concerned is required for regulations on` `any matter connected with the implementation of the Law`
#ASSERT NOT `s 60(1)(c) — consultation with the Minister concerned is required for regulations on` `the requirements of training for a licence`
#ASSERT NOT `s 60(1)(c) — consultation with the Minister concerned is required for regulations on` `the rules on the examinations required for a final certificate, including objections`
#ASSERT NOT `s 60(1)(c) — consultation with the Minister concerned is required for regulations on` `the manner of applying for a licence or its renewal, and the time for applying to renew`
#ASSERT NOT `s 60(1)(c) — consultation with the Minister concerned is required for regulations on` `the manner of applying for a temporary licence for a foreign expert, or for its renewal`

§§ `Section 60: the procedure followed, matter by matter`

-- 60(1) general, (a), (b): approval needed, consultation not.
#ASSERT `s 60 — the procedure required for regulations on` `any matter connected with the implementation of the Law` `has been followed, given the procedure` `approval only`
#ASSERT `s 60 — the procedure required for regulations on` `any matter connected with the implementation of the Law` `has been followed, given the procedure` `approval and consultation`
#ASSERT NOT `s 60 — the procedure required for regulations on` `any matter connected with the implementation of the Law` `has been followed, given the procedure` `neither approval nor consultation`
#ASSERT NOT `s 60 — the procedure required for regulations on` `any matter connected with the implementation of the Law` `has been followed, given the procedure` `consultation only`
#ASSERT `s 60 — the procedure required for regulations on` `the requirements of training for a licence` `has been followed, given the procedure` `approval only`
#ASSERT NOT `s 60 — the procedure required for regulations on` `the requirements of training for a licence` `has been followed, given the procedure` `consultation only`
#ASSERT `s 60 — the procedure required for regulations on` `the rules on the examinations required for a final certificate, including objections` `has been followed, given the procedure` `approval only`
#ASSERT NOT `s 60 — the procedure required for regulations on` `the rules on the examinations required for a final certificate, including objections` `has been followed, given the procedure` `neither approval nor consultation`

-- 60(1)(c): both needed; each alone is not enough.
#ASSERT `s 60 — the procedure required for regulations on` `the conditions for serving as testers or experts` `has been followed, given the procedure` `approval and consultation`
#ASSERT NOT `s 60 — the procedure required for regulations on` `the conditions for serving as testers or experts` `has been followed, given the procedure` `approval only`
#ASSERT NOT `s 60 — the procedure required for regulations on` `the conditions for serving as testers or experts` `has been followed, given the procedure` `consultation only`
#ASSERT NOT `s 60 — the procedure required for regulations on` `the conditions for serving as testers or experts` `has been followed, given the procedure` `neither approval nor consultation`

-- 60(2)(a), (b): no approval and no consultation, so the procedure is followed in every case.
#ASSERT `s 60 — the procedure required for regulations on` `the manner of applying for a licence or its renewal, and the time for applying to renew` `has been followed, given the procedure` `neither approval nor consultation`
#ASSERT `s 60 — the procedure required for regulations on` `the manner of applying for a licence or its renewal, and the time for applying to renew` `has been followed, given the procedure` `approval and consultation`
#ASSERT `s 60 — the procedure required for regulations on` `the manner of applying for a temporary licence for a foreign expert, or for its renewal` `has been followed, given the procedure` `neither approval nor consultation`
#ASSERT `s 60 — the procedure required for regulations on` `the manner of applying for a temporary licence for a foreign expert, or for its renewal` `has been followed, given the procedure` `consultation only`

-- The power, exercised or not (a MAY: unused is not a breach).
#TRACE `s 60 — the Minister's power to make regulations on` `the conditions for serving as testers or experts` `, given the procedure` `approval and consultation` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `make regulations on a matter` `the conditions for serving as testers or experts` AT 3
#TRACE `s 60 — the Minister's power to make regulations on` `the conditions for serving as testers or experts` `, given the procedure` `approval only` AT 0 WITH
    -- consultation missing: no permission
#TRACE `s 60 — the Minister's power to make regulations on` `the manner of applying for a licence or its renewal, and the time for applying to renew` `, given the procedure` `neither approval nor consultation` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `make regulations on a matter` `the manner of applying for a licence or its renewal, and the time for applying to renew` AT 2

§§ `Fork F-R-2: paragraph (1) read as covering the matters of paragraph (2) (alternative, not taken)`

-- On this reading the committee's approval is required for every matter, 60(2)(a) and (b) included.
#ASSERT `s 60 — reading paragraph (1) as covering the matters of paragraph (2), the approval of the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee is required for regulations on` `the manner of applying for a licence or its renewal, and the time for applying to renew`
#ASSERT `s 60 — reading paragraph (1) as covering the matters of paragraph (2), the approval of the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee is required for regulations on` `the manner of applying for a temporary licence for a foreign expert, or for its renewal`
-- The discriminating case: regulations on the manner of applying for a licence made WITHOUT the committee's approval.
-- Followed on the reading taken (paragraph (2) governs), not followed on the alternative.
#ASSERT `s 60 — the procedure required for regulations on` `the manner of applying for a licence or its renewal, and the time for applying to renew` `has been followed, given the procedure` `neither approval nor consultation`
#ASSERT NOT `s 60 — reading paragraph (1) as covering the matters of paragraph (2), the procedure required for regulations on` `the manner of applying for a licence or its renewal, and the time for applying to renew` `has been followed, given the procedure` `neither approval nor consultation`
#ASSERT `s 60 — reading paragraph (1) as covering the matters of paragraph (2), the procedure required for regulations on` `the manner of applying for a licence or its renewal, and the time for applying to renew` `has been followed, given the procedure` `approval only`
-- For the matters of paragraph (1) the two readings agree.
#ASSERT NOT `s 60 — reading paragraph (1) as covering the matters of paragraph (2), the procedure required for regulations on` `the requirements of training for a licence` `has been followed, given the procedure` `neither approval nor consultation`
#ASSERT `s 60 — reading paragraph (1) as covering the matters of paragraph (2), the procedure required for regulations on` `the conditions for serving as testers or experts` `has been followed, given the procedure` `approval and consultation`
#ASSERT NOT `s 60 — reading paragraph (1) as covering the matters of paragraph (2), the procedure required for regulations on` `the conditions for serving as testers or experts` `has been followed, given the procedure` `approval only`

§§ `Section 60(2)(a): the time for an application to renew (kind X)`

-- No regulation is in the sources: the time is not known, a named refusal, never a default.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 60(2)(a) — the last day for an application to renew a licence` NOTHING `the calendar with Saturday 21 March 2026 as a day of rest` BECAUSE "s 60(2)(a) fixes the time for an application to renew by regulations, and no regulation under section 60(2)(a) is in the sources"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 60(2)(a) — the last day for an application to renew a licence, IL s.10(c) not applied` NOTHING BECAUSE "s 60(2)(a) fixes the time for an application to renew by regulations, and no regulation under section 60(2)(a) is in the sources"
-- A regulation gives a nominal last day, Tuesday 31.3.2026, not a day of rest: that day.
#ASSERT `s 60(2)(a) — the last day for an application to renew a licence` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 31)) `the calendar with Saturday 21 March 2026 as a day of rest` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 31
-- A nominal last day on Saturday 21.3.2026, a day of rest: IL s.10(c) moves it to Sunday 22.3.2026 (ruling 4: a deadline).
#ASSERT `s 60(2)(a) — the last day for an application to renew a licence` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 21)) `the calendar with Saturday 21 March 2026 as a day of rest` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 22
-- The alternative without IL s.10(c) keeps the nominal day.
#ASSERT `s 60(2)(a) — the last day for an application to renew a licence, IL s.10(c) not applied` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 21)) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 21
#ASSERT `s 60(2)(a) — the last day for an application to renew a licence, IL s.10(c) not applied` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 31)) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 31
